config ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY
    bool "Prioritize the selected BLE HID host connection"
    depends on ZMK_BLE && BT_PERIPHERAL
    depends on !ZMK_SPLIT || ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL
    default n
    help
      The selected BLE HID endpoint requests the configured peripheral
      preference. Other known host links request latency 30, including while
      application data is transferred. USB means no selected BLE HID host.
      Split links, unknown hosts and other local identities are excluded.
      Does not require Studio or Messenger and does not change bonds,
      advertising, PHY, packet sizes or supervision timeout. Remote hosts
      decide actual parameters; requests are bounded and event driven.

config ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY_LOG_LEVEL
    int "BLE link policy log level"
    range 0 4
    default 3
    help
      Numeric slot and connection-parameter observations only; no addresses,
      input values, message contents or authentication data.

config ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY_DIAGNOSTICS
    bool "Record bounded link worker and API wall times"
    depends on ZMK_BLE_LINK_POLICY && LOG
    default n
    help
      Emit one numeric linkwork record after a worker that issued a request.
      Records worker/API wall time, request count, logical host mask, selected
      slot and pending delay. No payload, address, heap, new thread or timer.
      Clock samples use the system cycle counter and exclude the final summary
      log's own cost. This is not CPU, radio airtime or host HID delivery timing.
